        "So which one is more realistic? question/scenario 3, because real-world data, especially from experiments or observations, almost always contains some degree of variability, noise, or measurement error. It is extremely rare to find a dataset where a simple linear model can explain 100% of the variance (R-squared = 1) and have no residual error (SSE = 0). The non-zero SSE and R-squared value slightly less than 1 in scenario 3 reflect these realistic conditions where factors beyond the independent variable x influence the dependent variable y.\"\"\""
